{
	"_doc": "Repaint of Kenney's 512x512 blaster-kit colormap (variation-a layout). Each swatch rect [x0,y0,x1,y1] gets a role; a role is a top->bottom gradient (the source swatch's own luminance ramp picks the position) plus optional 'glow_band' = [t0,t1] slice of the gradient (0=top,1=bottom) that becomes the emissive energy accent (side faces span the ramp, so a mid band reads as a glowing strip; top faces sit at t~0 and stay metal), or 'glow_top': 1.0 for fully glowing swatches. 'ACCENT' in a colour means the blaster's accent colour; 'mix(a,b,t)' blends. Used by tools/art/blender/palette.py.",
	"source": ".cache/assets/blaster-kit/Models/Textures/variation-a.png",
	"default_role": "gunmetal",
	"roles": {
		"gunmetal": {
			"top": "#6a7079",
			"bottom": "#2c3037"
		},
		"steel": {
			"top": "#9aa0a8",
			"bottom": "#50555d"
		},
		"dark_steel": {
			"top": "#4a4e56",
			"bottom": "#24272c"
		},
		"polymer": {
